POWDER PRODUCTION PROCESS
Fig. 1 shows schematically the high-pressure water atomization process used in this experiment. Raw materials are melted in a high-frequency melting furnace. The hot metal is charged into the tundish with a nozzle hole provided at the bottom, through which the hot metal flows down. A water jet pressurized up to 70MPa by high-pressure pumps sprays the hot metal stream to atomize it. The powders produced are dehydrated by a filter press, then heated and dried in a vacuum. The dried powders are classified by an air classifier according to the users' requirements.
